        new("r-b1-2", "B1", new ComprehensionExercise(
            "How the Bicycle Changed Everyday Life",
            "Today the bicycle seems like a simple machine, but when it became popular in the late nineteenth century, it changed daily life in surprising ways.\n\nEarly bicycles were difficult and even dangerous to ride. One famous model had a huge front wheel and a tiny back wheel, and riders often fell from a great height. In the 1880s, however, engineers designed the \"safety bicycle\", with two wheels of the same size and a chain that turned the back wheel. This design is very close to the bicycles we ride today.\n\nSuddenly, ordinary workers could travel much further than they could walk. People living in villages could reach factories and markets in nearby towns, and young people could meet friends from other places. Some historians even say the bicycle helped people find partners outside their own village.\n\nThe bicycle also gave women more freedom. They could travel alone, and many started to wear more practical clothes for riding. Cycling clubs appeared in many countries, and the demand for smooth roads grew, which later helped the first car drivers.\n\nSo the next time you see a bicycle, remember that this quiet machine once caused a small revolution.",
            [
                new("What is the main idea of the text?", ["The bicycle had a big effect on how people lived", "Early bicycles were too dangerous to use", "Cars are more useful than bicycles", "How to repair an old bicycle"], 0, "The first sentence says the bicycle \"changed daily life in surprising ways\", and the text gives examples."),
